n=5: distribution of #distinct-eigenvalues over 1024 tournaments: {1: 120, 3: 664, 4: 240}
  transitive (nullcone vertex, char poly x^5): #distinct eigenvalues = 1 (=1, spectrum {0}), |Aut|=1
  |Aut| -> avg #distinct eigenvalues: {1: 3.0, 3: 3.0, 5: 3.0}
  => NULLCONE (transitive) = 1 distinct eigenvalue = MAXIMAL spectral degeneracy, but |Aut|=1 (rigid).
     LARGE |Aut| (symmetric) ALSO forces spectral degeneracy (fewer distinct) -- BUT via the
     semisimple/critical-line pole (Paley), not the nilpotent one. Two routes to degeneracy:
     nilpotent (transitive, GIT big-parabolic-stabilizer) vs symmetric (Paley, big S_n-Aut).
